Dependent triple plus pairwise independent pairs gives membership in span(A,B) by finCons independence criterion. Zero coefficient would place D in the span of one of the two vectors, contradicting the corresponding independent pair. Nonzero scaling lemma converts any relation to coefficients g_i*a_i then cancels each nonzero scalar. Scope is generic complex modules, no finite dimension assumption needed.
